{{!-- NO `.md-shell` OR `.md-workspace` WRAPPER HERE, DELIBERATELY.

     `user.supervision` is not a bare route -- it is in `accountRailContext`
     (controllers/user.js) -- so templates/user.hbs has ALREADY wrapped this outlet in
     `.md-shell md-shell--user`, the `md-shell--user-rail` modifier that reserves the account
     rail's 208px, a `.md-workspace`, and a `<main class="md-main md-main--user">`.

     This template used to declare its own copy of all of that. The result was two nested
     shells both carrying `padding-left: 208px` (app.scss, the `min-width: 901px` block), so
     the page's content sat exactly 208px right of where every sibling page sits -- the
     off-centre "My Supervisors" card. Measured at a 1440px viewport before the fix: outer
     shell x=0, inner shell x=280, modal body centred at 928 against a viewport centre of 720.

     THE RULE: a bare route brings its own shell (user/boards.hbs, user/stats.hbs and
     user/board-detail.hbs each do, correctly, and they are all in BARE_ROUTE_BASES). Every
     other user.* page takes the one templates/user.hbs provides and starts straight in with
     its content, exactly as goals/recordings/preferences/subscription/edit do.
     Guarded by scripts/account-rail-pages-qa.mjs, which fails if a page renders more than
     one `.md-shell`. --}}
{{!-- THE SAME COMPONENT THE MODAL USES, in `standalone` mode. ModalDialog drops its overlay
     and dialog chrome in that mode and yields the body into a plain container, so every list,
     control and action on this page is literally the modal's markup rather than a port of it.
     That is what keeps the two from drifting: one body, not two.

     The heading lives here, not in the component: the component's own title is modal furniture
     ("Supervision Settings for <user>"), and a page in this section should read like its
     siblings. --}}
<h2 class="md-supervision-page__title">{{t "Supervision" key="supervision"}}</h2>
<SupervisionSettings @model={{this.model}} @standalone={{true}} />
